Method Output enum Accessor Values <code>accountSummary</code> <code>EnumAccountTradeMode</code> <code>account_trade_mode()</code> <code>ACCOUNT_TRADE_MODE_DEMO</code> (0) / <code>CONTEST</code> (1) / <code>REAL</code> (2) <code>accountSummary</code> <code>EnumAccountMarginMode</code> <code>account_margin_mode()</code> <code>ACCOUNT_MARGIN_MODE_RETAIL_NETTING</code> (0) / <code>EXCHANGE</code> (1) / <code>RETAIL_HEDGING</code> (2) <pre><code>pb::AccountSummaryData s = account.accountSummary();
switch (s.account_trade_mode()) {
    case pb::ACCOUNT_TRADE_MODE_DEMO: std::puts("Demo account"); break;
    case pb::ACCOUNT_TRADE_MODE_REAL: std::puts("Real account"); break;
    default: break;
}
</code></pre>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::EquityHistoryRequest&amp;</code> Optional <code>from</code> / <code>from_utc</code>, <code>exclude_same_bars</code>. <pre><code>pb::EquityHistoryRequest req;
req.set_exclude_same_bars(true);
// req.set_from_utc("2026-01-01T00:00:00");
pb::EquityHistoryData h = account.equityHistory(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::TradeStatsRequest&amp;</code> Optional <code>from</code> / <code>from_utc</code> start; omit for all. <pre><code>pb::TradeStatsRequest req;                 // no `from` → full account history
// req.set_from_utc("2026-01-01T00:00:00"); // or from a date
pb::StatsData s = account.tradeStats(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::TradeStatsEquityHistoryRequest&amp;</code> Optional <code>from</code> / <code>from_utc</code>, <code>exclude_same_bars</code>. <pre><code>pb::TradeStatsEquityHistoryRequest req;
req.set_exclude_same_bars(true);
pb::StatsWithChartsData d = account.tradeStatsEquityHistory(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::TradeUnrealizedPLRequest&amp;</code> Optional <code>from</code> / <code>from_utc</code> start. <pre><code>pb::TradeUnrealizedPLRequest req;          // full life of each open order
pb::TradeUnrealizedPLData d = account.tradeUnrealizedPL(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OpenedOrdersRequest&amp;</code> Carries <code>sort_type</code>. Pass <code>{}</code> for <code>SORT_BY_OPEN_TIME_ASC</code>. <pre><code>pb::OpenedOrdersRequest req;
req.set_sort_type(pb::SORT_BY_OPEN_TIME_DESC);   // newest first
pb::OpenedOrdersData oo = account.openedOrders(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. The per-call deadline comes from <code>ClientOptions::unaryTimeoutMs</code> (default <code>30000</code> ms); transient failures are retried with back-off and a dropped terminal is re-attached automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OrdersHistoryRequest&amp;</code> The window, sort mode and paging. See fields above. <pre><code>#include &lt;google/protobuf/util/time_util.h&gt;
using google::protobuf::util::TimeUtil;

pb::OrdersHistoryRequest req;
req.set_input_sort_mode(pb::HISTORY_SORT_BY_CLOSE_TIME_DESC);     // newest closes first
*req.mutable_input_from_utc() = TimeUtil::SecondsToTimestamp(fromUnix);
*req.mutable_input_to_utc()   = TimeUtil::SecondsToTimestamp(toUnix);
req.set_items_per_page(100);
req.set_page_number(0);

pb::OrdersHistoryData h = account.ordersHistory(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. This call uses twice the normal <code>unaryTimeoutMs</code> because histories can be large; transient failures retry with back-off.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::QuoteHistoryBarsRequest&amp;</code> Symbol, timeframe, window, paging. <pre><code>#include &lt;ctime&gt;
int64_t now  = (int64_t)std::time(nullptr);
int64_t from = now - 7 * 24 * 3600;        // last week

pb::QuoteHistoryBarsRequest req;
req.set_symbol("EURUSD");
req.set_timeframe(pb::QHB_PERIOD_H1);      // H1 = 60 here!
req.set_from_time_utc(from);               // REQUIRED
req.set_to_time_utc(now);
req.set_page_size(500);

pb::QuoteHistoryBarsData d = account.bars(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::QuoteRequest&amp;</code> Carries <code>symbol</code>. Set it before calling. <pre><code>pb::QuoteRequest req;
req.set_symbol("EURUSD");
pb::QuoteData d = account.quote(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. The deadline comes from <code>ClientOptions::unaryTimeoutMs</code>; transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::QuoteHistoryRequest&amp;</code> Symbol, timeframe and window (see fields). <pre><code>#include &lt;google/protobuf/util/time_util.h&gt;
using google::protobuf::util::TimeUtil;

pb::QuoteHistoryRequest req;
req.set_symbol("EURUSD");
req.set_timeframe(pb::QH_PERIOD_H1);                              // H1 = 4 here!
*req.mutable_fromtimeutc() = TimeUtil::SecondsToTimestamp(fromUnix);
*req.mutable_totimeutc()   = TimeUtil::SecondsToTimestamp(toUnix);

pb::QuoteHistoryData h = account.quoteHistory(req);
</code></pre> <p>Accessor note: the proto field <code>fromTimeUtc</code> lowercases to <code>mutable_fromtimeutc()</code> / <code>fromtimeutc()</code>.</p> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::QuoteManyRequest&amp;</code> Repeated <code>symbols</code>. Add each with <code>add_symbols(...)</code>. <pre><code>pb::QuoteManyRequest req;
for (const char* s : {"EURUSD", "GBPUSD", "XAUUSD"}) req.add_symbols(s);
pb::QuoteManyData d = account.quoteMany(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. The deadline comes from <code>ClientOptions::unaryTimeoutMs</code>; transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::SymbolParamsManyRequest&amp;</code> Set <code>symbol_name</code> for one symbol; leave unset for all. <pre><code>pb::SymbolParamsManyRequest req;
req.set_symbol_name("EURUSD");        // or leave unset → every symbol
pb::SymbolParamsManyData d = account.symbolParamsMany(req);
const pb::SymbolParamsManyInfo&amp; s = d.symbol_infos(0);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::SymbolSelectRequest&amp;</code> <code>symbol</code> + <code>select</code> (true to add, false to remove). <pre><code>pb::SymbolSelectRequest req;
req.set_symbol("EURUSD");
req.set_select(true);
bool ok = account.symbolSelect(req).success();
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::TickValueWithSizeRequest&amp;</code> Repeated <code>symbol_names</code>. Add with <code>add_symbol_names(...)</code>. <pre><code>pb::TickValueWithSizeRequest req;
req.add_symbol_names("EURUSD");
req.add_symbol_names("XAUUSD");
pb::TickValueWithSizeData d = account.tickValueWithSize(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Transient failures retry automatically.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OrderCloseByRequest&amp;</code> The two tickets: the one to close + the opposite one. <pre><code>pb::OrderCloseByRequest req;
req.set_ticket_to_close(buyTicket);
req.set_opposite_ticket_closing_by(sellTicket);
pb::OrderCloseByData r = account.orderCloseBy(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Trades use <code>ClientOptions::tradeTimeoutMs</code>.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OrderCloseDeleteRequest&amp;</code> Ticket (+ optional lots/closing_price/slippage for market). <pre><code>pb::OrderCloseDeleteRequest req;
req.set_order_ticket(ticket);
// full close: leave lots unset. Partial: req.set_lots(0.05);
pb::OrderCloseDeleteData r = account.orderCloseDelete(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Trades use <code>ClientOptions::tradeTimeoutMs</code>.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OrderModifyRequest&amp;</code> Ticket + the field(s) to change. <pre><code>pb::OrderModifyRequest req;
req.set_order_ticket(ticket);
req.set_new_stop_loss(1.09500);
req.set_new_take_profit(1.10500);
bool ok = account.orderModify(req).order_was_modified();
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Trades use <code>ClientOptions::tradeTimeoutMs</code>.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OrderSendRequest&amp;</code> Symbol, operation, volume, optional price/SL/TP/slippage/magic/comment/expiry. <pre><code>pb::OrderSendRequest req;
req.set_symbol("EURUSD");
req.set_operation_type(pb::OC_OP_BUY);
req.set_volume(0.10);
req.set_slippage(10);               // 10 points
// optional: req.set_stoploss(...); req.set_takeprofit(...); req.set_magic_number(777);
pb::OrderSendData r = account.orderSend(req);
</code></pre> <p>There is no <code>ctx</code> parameter. Trades use <code>ClientOptions::tradeTimeoutMs</code> (separate from read RPCs); tune via <code>account.options()</code>.</p> <p>⚠️ Not safe to blindly retry. On a transport timeout the order may already be live. Re-query OpenedOrders before resending.</p>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OnConnectStateRequest&amp;</code> <code>terminal_ids</code> to watch; leave empty for this session's terminal. <code>callback</code> <code>std::function&lt;void(const pb::ConnectStateData&amp;)&gt;</code> Invoked on each state change, on a background thread. <pre><code>pb::OnConnectStateRequest req;             // empty → this terminal
auto stream = account.onConnectState(req, [](const pb::ConnectStateData&amp; s) { /* ... */ });
</code></pre>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OnOpenedOrdersProfitRequest&amp;</code> Set <code>timer_period_milliseconds</code> (e.g. <code>1000</code>). <code>callback</code> <code>std::function&lt;void(const pb::OnOpenedOrdersProfitData&amp;)&gt;</code> Invoked per snapshot, on a background thread. <pre><code>pb::OnOpenedOrdersProfitRequest req;
req.set_timer_period_milliseconds(1000);     // once per second
auto stream = account.onOpenedOrdersProfit(req, [](const pb::OnOpenedOrdersProfitData&amp; d) { /* ... */ });
</code></pre>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OnOpenedOrdersTicketsRequest&amp;</code> Set <code>pull_interval_milliseconds</code> (e.g. <code>1000</code>). <code>callback</code> <code>std::function&lt;void(const pb::OnOpenedOrdersTicketsData&amp;)&gt;</code> Invoked per snapshot, on a background thread. <pre><code>pb::OnOpenedOrdersTicketsRequest req;
req.set_pull_interval_milliseconds(1000);
auto stream = account.onOpenedOrdersTickets(req, [](const pb::OnOpenedOrdersTicketsData&amp; d) { /* ... */ });
</code></pre>

Parameter Type Description <code>req</code> <code>const pb::OnSymbolTickRequest&amp;</code> <code>symbol_names</code> to subscribe to (<code>add_symbol_names</code>). <code>callback</code> <code>std::function&lt;void(const pb::OnSymbolTickData&amp;)&gt;</code> Invoked per tick, on a background thread. <pre><code>pb::OnSymbolTickRequest req;
req.add_symbol_names("EURUSD");
req.add_symbol_names("GBPUSD");
auto stream = account.onSymbolTick(req, [](const pb::OnSymbolTickData&amp; d) { /* ... */ });
</code></pre> <p>Select the symbols first (SymbolSelect) so the terminal is subscribed to them.</p>
